  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 501(c)(3), private inurement applies specifically to insiders (founders, officers, directors, and persons with substantial influence), while the private benefit doctrine covers outsiders. The consultant is an outsider receiving excessive compensation, constituting private benefit. The executive director is an insider, so the no-interest personal loan constitutes private inurement.
