Wrong (B): The private benefit doctrine applies to the consultant (an outsider), but the personal loan to the executive director is specifically private inurement because the director is an insider. The two doctrines are distinct.
Wrong (D): Section 4958 intermediate sanctions apply to disqualified persons (insiders), not to outside contractors. Additionally, a $50,000 no-interest personal loan is not a de minimis fringe benefit.$EXPL$
